    <div class="kpi-value amber">48.8%</div>
    <div class="kpi-detail">91 sellers (5.2% of total)</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 1: Market Overview -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">1</div>
    <h2>Market Overview & Listing Composition</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="section-intro">The secondary smartwatch market is heavily concentrated around Apple, which accounts for nearly two-thirds of all listings. The U.S. dominates geographic distribution at 65%, with the UK as a distant second at 13%.</p>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Brand Distribution</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartBrandDist" height="260"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Condition Mix</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartCondDist" height="260"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row full">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Top 10 Countries by Listing Volume</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartCountryDist" height="200"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight">
    <strong>Key finding:</strong> 43.1% of listings are labeled "New" — surprising for a secondary market. This suggests authorized resellers and gray-market dealers are significant participants, not just individuals offloading used watches. The 27.3% worldwide-shipping rate enables cross-border arbitrage.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: Brand Pricing -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">2</div>
    <h2>Brand-Level Pricing & Value Retention</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="section-intro">Garmin commands the highest median resale price at $567, followed by Apple at $550 and Samsung at $530. However, the real story is in price variance: Samsung has the widest dispersion, with extreme high-end listings pulling its mean far above the median.</p>

  <div class="chart-row full">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Price Distribution by Brand (99th percentile cap for clarity)</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartBrandBox" height="280"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table style="margin-top:20px">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Brand</th>
